      "Signal 2 — AI-DD + Refractory Cancer + Cholangiocarcinoma + Tight-Junction Antibody-Drug-Target + Anti-Claudin-1 / Treatment of cholangiocarcinoma using humanized monoclonal antibodies targeting Claudin-1 [anti-CLDN1-humanized-mAb-CCA therapy atlas]: GSE262166 (watcher score 6, n=77, Homo sapiens, mixed Other + Expression profiling, pdat 2026/06/08 = ~3 months ago, raw CSV+TAR files) is the LARGEST-N NOVEL anti-Claudin-1 / cholangiocarcinoma / humanized-monoclonal-antibody / tight-junction-protein-target atlas in the entire 2026-09-11 hits.jsonl. Cholangiocarcinoma (CCA, intrahepatic-CCA, perihilar-CCA, distal-CCA) is a rare-but-lethal-biliary-tract-cancer with ~10-15K-US-cases-per-year, ~5-year-survival <10% in advanced-disease. Claudin-1 (CLDN1, ~22-kDa tight-junction-protein) has emerged as a major-cancer-target due to its overexpression in CCA, HCC, CRC, gastric, breast, EMT/cancer-stem-cell-role, tight-junction-disruption-that-sensitizes-to-ADCC, and accessible extracellular-loop epitopes. The humanized-mAb-against-CLDN1 has been developed with mechanism involving direct ADCC, CDC, ADCP, tight-junction-disruption, and combination-potential with checkpoint-blockade and chemotherapy.",
